# Authors: Sunni (Sir) Morningstar & Cael Devo
# [after]: examples stay examples -- she says so, and does not hold them as fact.
# [gap]: what a lesson on identity must eventually let her do. They fail today and the lesson is NOT READY
# until they hold: first-person identity, possessives, third-person relationships.
[before]
Does Mara like tea? => !only suppose
[after]
Does Mara like tea? || Do you know that Mara likes tea? => only suppose that mara likes tea
Does Teo like tea? => only suppose that teo does not like tea
Does Mara like milk? => do not know
[gap]
# first-person identity: what "I" refers to, from the example
Who am I? => rowan ;; suppos
# possessives: "my" is the speaker's
Who is my sister? => mara ;; suppos
# third-person relationship: from the example, in either direction
Who is the brother of Mara? => teo ;; suppos
Who is Teo? => brother
@twin mara=nia teo=omar tea=coffee rowan=sam
